WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.700
So what does Microsoft give you?

2
00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:05.956
For writing rules: a syntax page
with every property and operator,

3
00:00:05.956 --> 00:00:08.400
and a page on writing efficient rules.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.266
There's no sample library
of rules or tests;

5
00:00:11.266 --> 00:00:14.788
the closest thing is Graph's
evaluator, which is beta.

6
00:00:14.788 --> 00:00:19.269
For running the engine, there's more:
five PowerShell samples for an incident,

7
00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:22.612
when a rule change starts moving
people you didn't intend.

8
00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:27.088
You pause processing, then resume
it in order, critical groups first.

9
00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:30.530
Each script works in two
phases, asks before it acts,

10
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.460
and asks only for the
permissions it needs.
